; claude: XPM, pictures as text (a palette and rows of characters),
; read and written by our own code: the sprites' file format (see
; Xpm.mli, and Sprite.of_xpm). Pure OCaml, like png/, gif/ and jpeg/
; (graphics_images, which loads them, needs Unix's sockets), so the web
; backend can use it too. A private library (see
; graphics/core/dune), installed as part of elm_playground, whose
; Sprite uses it.
(library
 (name graphics_xpm)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
)
